\ native-cross.4 - the native back end's cross compiler (docs/NATIVE.md,
\ N1c-1; Iteration 616 begins it). It builds on forth/cross-core.4, as
\ cross.4 does - the vocabularies, the target dictionary space, the
\ headers - and lays native code into the same image through
\ forth/asm64.4 and forth/native.4. Run from the repository's top:
\     ./relf64 forth/kernel64.img < forth/native-n1c.4
\
\ The image: cross-core's IMAGE, a buffer of offsets from the image's
\ start, as CV8's images are. asm64 is pointed at it with ORG 0, so a
\ call's rel32 is between offsets, and the code does not care where the
\ image is loaded. Two positions, kept in step whenever one hands over to
\ the other: cross-core's DP-T, where headers and data go, and asm64's
\ THERE, where code goes - N>A and A>N.
\
\ The file: an ELF executable - a page holding the ELF header, then the
\ image, mapped at N-BASE: so N-BASE is START, the image's base at run
\ time, and the target's absolute addresses are N-BASE plus an offset.

VARIABLE TARGET-CELL-BYTES  8 TARGET-CELL-BYTES !   \ x86-64: 8, always
S" forth/cross-core.4" INCLUDED
S" forth/asm64.4" INCLUDED
S" forth/native.4" INCLUDED
ALSO ASSEMBLER
DECIMAL

4198400 CONSTANT N-BASE            \ 0x401000: the image, after the header page
N-BASE N-START !                   \ @XT and !XT count from it
IMAGE ABUF !  0 ORG !  IMAGE THERE !
\ A prologue: nothing real at offset 0, which means "none" to PRIMITIVE and
\ cross-core's links alike - MOVE, native-rt.4's first routine, was laid
\ there and taken for "no routine", and got a stub (Iteration 620).
: N-PROLOGUE ( --- )  16 0 DO 204 C,A LOOP  16 DP-T ! ;   \ int3: a jump there traps
N-PROLOGUE                                   \ (a loop is compile-only at the top level)

\ (674) The kernel's own data in data's region, as kernel-native.4's CREATE
\ puts the shell's (672): DP-T and N-DDP-T trade places, so ,-T C,-T and
\ ALLOT-T lay data after a VARIABLE, until N-HEAD or N>A swaps them back.
VARIABLE N-DDP-T      \ the other target pointer: set where N-DSTART is
VARIABLE N-IN-DATA
: N-DATA-SWAP ( --- )   DP-T @  N-DDP-T @ DP-T !  N-DDP-T ! ;
: N-DATA-ON ( --- )   N-IN-DATA @ 0= IF  N-DATA-SWAP  -1 N-IN-DATA !  THEN ;
: N-DATA-OFF ( --- )   N-IN-DATA @ IF  N-DATA-SWAP  0 N-IN-DATA !  THEN ;
: N>A ( --- )  N-DATA-OFF  IMAGE DP-T @ + THERE ! ;      \ code goes where the target is
: A>N ( --- )  THERE @ IMAGE - DP-T ! ;      \ and the target goes on after it
: N-ABS ( t-addr --- addr )  N-BASE + ;     \ a target offset's address at run time

\ NH: name ... N;  - a native colon definition with a target header: the
\ header (cross-core's "HEADER, threaded as the target's FIND will look),
\ then the body, native code, compiled by native.4's N-COMPILE. Its shadow
\ is in NTARGET and answers the body's offset, so later words call it.
: NH: ( "name" --- )
  CURRENT @ >R  NTARGET CURRENT !  "HEADER  R> CURRENT !
  DP-T @ ,
  N>A  HERE-A N-SELF !  N-COMPILE  A>N
  DOES> @ call, ;

\ ---- the ELF file ------------------------------------------------------------
CREATE N-EHDR 4096 ALLOT                     \ the header page
: E! ( x offset bytes --- )   \ little-endian, into the header page
  0 DO  2DUP N-EHDR + I + SWAP 255 AND SWAP C!  SWAP 8 RSHIFT SWAP  LOOP 2DROP ;
VARIABLE N-MEMSZ   4194304 N-MEMSZ !         \ the image and what follows it: stacks
\ - 4 MB, the asm engine's MEMSIZE, its layout at the top (639): the return
\ stack, the image's own (64 KB), the guard page between the stacks
\ (RGUARD), the data stack (256 KB) over its floor's guard (DGUARD); a
\ return stack overflow or a data stack underflow traps at RGUARD (-5), a
\ data stack overflow at DGUARD (-3). Below them the signal stack - the
\ trap handler runs there, as it must when the return stack is spent -
\ and below that the runtime's data, where the dictionary ends.
65536 CONSTANT N-RSTACK-BYTES   262144 CONSTANT N-DSTACK-BYTES   4096 CONSTANT N-PAGE
N-BASE N-MEMSZ @ + CONSTANT N-RTOP
N-RTOP N-RSTACK-BYTES - CONSTANT N-RFLOOR
N-RFLOOR N-PAGE - CONSTANT N-RGUARD          \ the engine's MEMSIZE - RS - PAGE
N-RGUARD CONSTANT N-DTOP
N-RFLOOR N-DSTACK-BYTES - CONSTANT N-DGUARD  \ the engine's MEMSIZE - RS - DS
N-DGUARD N-PAGE + CONSTANT N-DFLOOR
N-DGUARD 32768 - CONSTANT N-SIGSTK           \ 32 KB for the signal handlers
\ (672) The data's own region: 512 KB below the runtime's 64 KB, where
\ CREATE puts the data and the code never goes - so the code's pages stay
\ as the file has them. The code grows from the image's start up to it.
N-SIGSTK 65536 - 524288 - CONSTANT N-DSTART
N-SIGSTK 8 - CONSTANT N-DLIMIT               \ the runtime data's last cell: data's limit, or 0
N-DSTART N-BASE - N-DDP-T !                  \ (674) the kernel's own data begins there
: N-ELF ( entry-t-addr --- )   \ the header page, for an image of DP-T bytes
  N-EHDR 4096 0 FILL
  127 0 1 E!  69 1 1 E!  76 2 1 E!  70 3 1 E!  2 4 1 E!  1 5 1 E!  1 6 1 E!
  2 16 2 E!  62 18 2 E!  1 20 4 E!                  \ executable, x86-64, version 1
  N-ABS 24 8 E!                                     \ e_entry
  64 32 8 E!  0 40 8 E!  0 48 4 E!                  \ e_phoff, e_shoff, e_flags
  64 52 2 E!  56 54 2 E!  2 56 2 E!  64 58 2 E!  0 60 2 E!  0 62 2 E!
  1 64 4 E!  7 68 4 E!                              \ the code: PT_LOAD, rwx
  0 72 8 E!  N-BASE 4096 - DUP 80 8 E!  88 8 E!     \ from the file's start
  DP-T @ 4096 + 96 8 E!                             \ p_filesz
  N-DSTART N-BASE 4096 - - 104 8 E!  4096 112 8 E!  \ p_memsz, up to data's region
  1 120 4 E!  7 124 4 E!                            \ (672) the data: PT_LOAD, rwx
  DP-T @ 4096 + 4095 + -4096 AND 128 8 E!           \ the page after the code's
  N-DSTART DUP 136 8 E!  144 8 E!                   \ p_vaddr, p_paddr
  N-DDP-T @ N-DSTART N-BASE - - 152 8 E!           \ p_filesz: the kernel's own data (674)
  N-BASE N-MEMSZ @ + N-DSTART - 160 8 E!  4096 168 8 E! ;   \ the rest, the stacks
: WRITE-ELF ( c-addr u --- )   \ the header page, then the image - its code, its data
  N-DATA-OFF  2DUP W/O CREATE-FILE THROW >R
  N-EHDR 4096 R@ WRITE-FILE THROW
  IMAGE DP-T @ R@ WRITE-FILE THROW
  N-EHDR 4096 0 FILL  N-EHDR  DP-T @ 4096 + 4095 + -4096 AND  DP-T @ 4096 + -  R@ WRITE-FILE THROW
  IMAGE N-DSTART N-BASE - +  N-DDP-T @ N-DSTART N-BASE - -  R@ WRITE-FILE THROW   \ (674)
  R> CLOSE-FILE THROW  493 CHMOD THROW ;

\ ==== compiling kernel.4 (Iteration 618, N1c-1c) ==============================
\ kernel.4 begins with CROSS-COMPILE and ends with END-CROSS, as cross.4
\ reads it; here CROSS-COMPILE runs N-CROSS: at the top level the words
\ of NTRANS - the directives kernel.4 uses: PRIMITIVE OPCODE ESCAPED : ;
\ VARIABLE CONSTANT IMMEDIATE ALLOT-T and the like - and numbers on the
\ host's stack; inside a definition, native.4's N-COMPILE.

WORDLIST CONSTANT NTRANS

\ A shadow's cells: the address to call, a primitive's template (an
\ NPRIMS xt) or 0, and the target header's name field - its flags, for
\ POSTPONE (622). Found while compiling, it lays itself: the template
\ inline, or a call.
: N>BODY ( t-xt --- t-addr )   \ a created word's data: the address in its mov
  11 + DUP C@-T  OVER 1+ C@-T 8 LSHIFT OR  OVER 2 + C@-T 16 LSHIFT OR
  SWAP 3 + C@-T 24 LSHIFT OR  N-BASE - ;
: N-SHADOW ( pfa --- )   \ the second cell: -1 a VARIABLE, its address pushed
  \ inline; -2 a CONSTANT, the value in the fourth cell (627); else a template
  DUP CELL+ @  DUP -1 = IF DROP @ N>BODY N-ABS N-LIT EXIT THEN
  DUP -2 = IF DROP 3 CELLS + @ N-LIT EXIT THEN
  ?DUP IF NIP EXECUTE ELSE @ call, THEN ;
CREATE N-NAME 32 ALLOT                       \ the name being defined
: N-PEEK-NAME ( --- )   \ the next name, into N-NAME, the input left before it
  >IN @  BL WORD COUNT 31 MIN DUP N-NAME C!  N-NAME 1+ SWAP MOVE  >IN ! ;
: N-HEAD ( --- )   \ the header, and its shadow in NTARGET: CREATEd, cells to follow
  N-DATA-OFF                                                \ (674)
  N-PEEK-NAME  CURRENT @ >R  NTARGET CURRENT !  "HEADER  R> CURRENT ! ;

\ Calls to a word not defined yet - (.") and (ABORT") are used before
\ kernel.4 defines them: a call with no target, a node [next][fix][name]
\ remembering it, and the target patched when a word of that name comes.
VARIABLE N-FWDS
: N-FWD-CALL ( c-addr u --- )
  232 C,A  THERE @  0 L,A                    ( c-addr u fix )
  HERE >R  N-FWDS @ ,  ,  R> N-FWDS !
  DUP C,  0 ?DO DUP I + C@ C, LOOP DROP  ALIGN ;
: N-FWD-RESOLVE ( --- )   \ calls laid before N-NAME's definition: to here
  N-FWDS @ BEGIN ?DUP WHILE
    DUP CELL+ @ IF  DUP 2 CELLS + COUNT N-NAME COUNT COMPARE 0= IF
      DUP CELL+ @ N-RESOLVE  0 OVER CELL+ !  THEN  THEN
    @
  REPEAT ;
: N-CALL-NAMED ( c-addr u --- )   \ a call by name, now or when it comes
  2DUP NTARGET SEARCH-WORDLIST IF NIP NIP EXECUTE ELSE N-FWD-CALL THEN ;
: N-PAD-TO ( addr --- )  BEGIN HERE-A OVER < WHILE 144 C,A REPEAT DROP ;   \ nops
: N-STR, ( c-addr u --- )  DUP C,A  0 ?DO DUP I + C@ C,A LOOP DROP ;
CREATE N-DOTQ  4 C, 40 C, 46 C, 34 C, 41 C,            \ (.")
CREATE N-ABORTQ  8 C, 40 C, 65 C, 66 C, 79 C, 82 C, 84 C, 34 C, 41 C,   \ (ABORT")
CREATE N-SQ  4 C, 40 C, 83 C, 34 C, 41 C,              \ (S")
CREATE N-COMPILEC  8 C, 67 C, 79 C, 77 C, 80 C, 73 C, 76 C, 69 C, 44 C,   \ COMPILE,

\ inside definitions: kernel.4's cross-time words
CURRENT @  NCTRL CURRENT !
: CELLBYTES-TOK  8 N-LIT ;   : CELLSHIFT-TOK  3 N-LIT ;   : SIGNSHIFT-TOK  63 N-LIT ;
\ CV8's opcodes, as numbers: only CV8's back-end words use them, which the
\ native kernel replaces; a word compiled with them here is never run
: LIT32-TOK 0 N-LIT ;  : DOVAR-TOK 0 N-LIT ;  : DODOES-TOK 0 N-LIT ;  : LIT8-TOK 0 N-LIT ;
: BRANCH8-TOK 0 N-LIT ;  : 0BRANCH8-TOK 0 N-LIT ;
: [OP]  CR ." native-cross: [OP] - a CV8 back-end word reached the native compiler" CR BYE ;
: ."      N-DOTQ COUNT N-CALL-NAMED  34 WORD COUNT N-STR, ;
: ABORT"  N-ABORTQ COUNT N-CALL-NAMED  34 WORD COUNT N-STR, ;
: S"      N-SQ COUNT N-CALL-NAMED  34 WORD COUNT N-STR, ;     \ (619)
: [CHAR]  N-WORD 1+ C@ N-LIT ;                                  \ (620)
: [']   N-WORD COUNT NTARGET SEARCH-WORDLIST 0= IF                \ (623): native.4's, plus
    CR ." native-cross: ['] of no target word: " N-LASTWORD COUNT TYPE CR BYE THEN
  >BODY @ N-ABS N-LIT ;                                           \ the image's base
: POSTPONE   \ (622) common words of part 9 - [CHAR] ['] - POSTPONE LITERAL
  N-WORD COUNT NTARGET SEARCH-WORDLIST 0= IF
    CR ." native-cross: POSTPONE of a word not yet defined: " N-LASTWORD COUNT TYPE CR BYE THEN
  >BODY  DUP 2 CELLS + @ C@-T 64 AND IF       \ immediate: its run time, now
    N-SHADOW
  ELSE                                        \ else: its xt, and the target's COMPILE,
    @ N-ABS N-LIT  N-COMPILEC COUNT N-CALL-NAMED
  THEN ;
CURRENT !

\ the top level
: N-CROSS ( --- )
  BEGIN
    N-WORD
    DUP COUNT S" END-CROSS" COMPARE 0= IF DROP EXIT THEN
    DUP COUNT NTRANS SEARCH-WORDLIST IF NIP EXECUTE ELSE
    DUP NUMBER? IF DROP NIP ELSE
      2DROP CR ." native-cross: unknown at the top level: " COUNT TYPE CR BYE
    THEN THEN
  AGAIN ;
: CROSS-COMPILE ( --- )  N-CROSS ;

: N-STUB24 ( --- )   \ a created word's body, as kernel-native.4's CREATE lays it
  \ (623): sub rbp,8  mov [rbp],rbx  mov rbx,data  ret  - the ret at 15, where
  \ DOES> puts its jump - then nops to 24. The data begins at the next
  \ 64-byte boundary, int3 between (626): data written never shares a cache
  \ line with code - a store there is self-modifying code to the processor,
  \ a machine clear each time (NATIVE.md 9). The mov holds the address;
  \ >BODY reads it there.
  \ (674) The data in data's region now, as 672 put the shell's: no line.
  N-DDP-T @ 7 + -8 AND DUP N-DDP-T !  >R
  72 C,A 131 C,A 237 C,A 8 C,A  72 C,A 137 C,A 93 C,A 0 C,A
  72 C,A 199 C,A 195 C,A  R> N-ABS L,A  195 C,A  8 0 DO 144 C,A LOOP ;
CURRENT @  NTRANS CURRENT !
: \  SOURCE NIP >IN ! ;
: (  41 WORD DROP ;
: COLD ;  : WARM ;  : LOCALS-CELLS ;  : ESCAPED ;     \ CV8's boot vectors and band
: CHARS-T CHARS-T ;  : CELLS-T CELLS-T ;  : ALLOT-T ALLOT-T ;
: IMMEDIATE  TLINK @ DUP C@-T 64 OR SWAP C!-T ;
: PRIMITIVE ( "name" --- )
  \ the header; its body the template and ret, flagged inline, or a jump to
  \ the runtime's routine, or a stub that names itself and exits (99)
  N-PEEK-NAME
  N-NAME COUNT NPRIMS SEARCH-WORDLIST IF ELSE 0 THEN            ( template|0 )
  N-NAME COUNT NTARGET SEARCH-WORDLIST IF >BODY @ ELSE 0 THEN   ( template routine|0 )
  N-HEAD
  \ The shadow's two cells first, before any code: a template's forward
  \ local label (asm64's `1 F`) allots a record in the host's dictionary,
  \ and a cell stored after it lands after the record - ?DUP's did, and
  \ N-SHADOW executed what it read there (Iteration 619).
  OVER IF  DP-T @ ,  OVER ,  ELSE  DUP IF DUP , ELSE DP-T @ , THEN  0 ,  THEN
  TLINK @ ,                                    \ the third: its name field (622)
  N>A
  OVER IF                                     \ a template: its code, ret, inline
    \ EB 01 len: a jump over the length of the template (623) - the
    \ target's COMPILE, sees it and copies that many bytes, inline
    DROP  235 C,A 1 C,A  THERE @ >R  0 C,A
    EXECUTE  THERE @ R@ 1+ -  R> C!  195 C,A
    TLINK @ DUP C@-T 32 OR SWAP C!-T
  ELSE ?DUP IF                                \ a routine: jump to it; calls go there
    jmp,
  ELSE                                        \ neither: name itself on stderr, exit 99
    rsi TLINK @ 1+ N-ABS # mov,  edx TLINK @ C@-T 31 AND # mov,  edi 2 # mov,
    eax 1 # mov,  syscall,  edi 99 # mov,  eax 60 # mov,  syscall,
  THEN DROP THEN
  A>N
  DOES> N-SHADOW ;
: OPCODE ( n "name" --- )  DROP  S" PRIMITIVE" NTRANS SEARCH-WORDLIST DROP EXECUTE ;
: : ( "name" --- )
  N-HEAD  DP-T @ ,  0 ,  TLINK @ ,
  N>A  N-FWD-RESOLVE  HERE-A N-SELF !  N-COMPILE  A>N
  DOES> N-SHADOW ;
: VARIABLE ( "name" --- )   \ the 24-byte stub, then the cell
  N-HEAD  DP-T @ ,  -1 ,  TLINK @ ,
  N>A  N-STUB24  A>N  N-DATA-ON  0 ,-T
  DOES> N-SHADOW ;
: CONSTANT ( n "name" --- )
  N-HEAD  DP-T @ ,  -2 ,  TLINK @ ,  DUP ,
  N>A  N-PUSH  rbx SWAP # mov,  195 C,A  A>N
  DOES> N-SHADOW ;
CURRENT !

\ ==== kernel.4's back end: skipped here, compiled from kernel-native.4 (622)
\ The words of part 9 that lay CV8's code: their CV8 definitions are
\ skipped, name and body, and an IMMEDIATE after one with them; a call to
\ one from a common word before kernel-native.4 defines it is a forward
\ call, resolved when it does. Other unknown words still end the build.
: N-SUBST, ( "names" --- )  \ the rest of the line's names, into the list
  BEGIN BL WORD DUP C@ WHILE  COUNT DUP C,  0 ?DO DUP I + C@ C, LOOP DROP  REPEAT DROP ;
CREATE N-SUBST-LIST         \ after N-SUBST, - its data must follow its header
N-SUBST, OP, REWIND W, SLOT, NO-PEEP LIT, EXIT, CALL, PEEP-IMM PEEP-VAR DOES-FETCH? LIT-LEN CONST-WORD?
N-SUBST, INL-PLAIN? INL-OP INLINE-LEN SLOT@ INLINE-COPY INL-MAXI INL-MAXB
N-SUBST, COMPILE, ; CREATE CONSTANT OPERAND3@ (POSTPONE) : >MARK >RESOLVE BACK,
N-SUBST, BEGIN UNTIL AGAIN IF THEN ELSE WHILE REPEAT DO LEAVE-LINK, ?DO LEAVE
N-SUBST, RESOLVE-LEAVE LOOP +LOOP RECURSE POSTPONE >BODY (;CODE) DOES>
0 C,  ALIGN
: N-SUBST? ( c-addr u --- f )
  N-SUBST-LIST BEGIN DUP C@ WHILE
    >R  2DUP R@ COUNT COMPARE 0= IF 2DROP R> DROP TRUE EXIT THEN
    R> COUNT +
  REPEAT DROP 2DROP FALSE ;
VARIABLE N-SKIPPED                      \ the last definition was skipped
VARIABLE N-TRACE                        \ set: each definition's name is said
VARIABLE N-SKIPPING  -1 N-SKIPPING !     \ off while kernel-native.4 is compiled (623)
VARIABLE N-FWD-NAMES                    \ how many forward calls to the back end
: N-LATER? ( c-addr u --- f )   \ part 10's words part 9 calls: cross.4's FORWARDs
  2DUP S" WARM" COMPARE 0= >R  S" COLD" COMPARE 0=  R> OR ;
: N-SUBST-FWD ( c-addr --- f )          \ native.4's N-UNKNOWN: a forward call
  DUP COUNT N-SUBST? OVER COUNT N-LATER? OR
  IF COUNT N-FWD-CALL  1 N-FWD-NAMES +!  TRUE ELSE DROP FALSE THEN ;
: N-UNRESOLVED ( --- )   \ the forward calls still waiting, by name
  N-FWDS @ BEGIN ?DUP WHILE
    DUP CELL+ @ IF DUP 2 CELLS + COUNT TYPE SPACE THEN  @
  REPEAT ;
' N-SUBST-FWD N-UNKNOWN !
CREATE N-DQ  2 C, 46 C, 34 C,                          \ ."
CREATE N-SDQ  2 C, 83 C, 34 C,                         \ S"
CREATE N-ADQ  6 C, 65 C, 66 C, 79 C, 82 C, 84 C, 34 C,  \ ABORT"
: N-SKIP-NAME ( --- )  N-WORD DROP ;
: N-SKIP-DEF ( --- )   \ past the name, and the body to its ;
  N-SKIP-NAME
  BEGIN N-WORD
    DUP COUNT S" ;" COMPARE 0= IF DROP EXIT THEN
    DUP COUNT S" \" COMPARE 0= IF SOURCE NIP >IN ! THEN
    DUP COUNT S" (" COMPARE 0= IF 41 WORD DROP THEN
    DUP COUNT S" .(" COMPARE 0= IF 41 WORD DROP THEN
    DUP COUNT 2DUP N-DQ COUNT COMPARE 0= >R 2DUP N-SDQ COUNT COMPARE 0= >R
      N-ADQ COUNT COMPARE 0= R> OR R> OR IF 34 WORD DROP THEN     \ ." S" ABORT"
    DUP COUNT 2DUP S" POSTPONE" COMPARE 0= >R 2DUP S" [']" COMPARE 0= >R
      2DUP S" '" COMPARE 0= >R 2DUP S" CHAR" COMPARE 0= >R S" [CHAR]" COMPARE 0=
      R> OR R> OR R> OR R> OR IF N-SKIP-NAME THEN
    DROP
  AGAIN ;
CURRENT @  NTRANS CURRENT !
: IMMEDIATE  N-SKIPPED @ IF 0 N-SKIPPED ! ELSE TLINK @ DUP C@-T 64 OR SWAP C!-T THEN ;
: : ( "name" --- )
  N-PEEK-NAME  N-TRACE @ IF N-NAME COUNT TYPE SPACE THEN
  N-SKIPPING @ IF N-NAME COUNT N-SUBST? IF N-SKIP-DEF  -1 N-SKIPPED ! EXIT THEN THEN
  0 N-SKIPPED !
  N-HEAD  DP-T @ ,  0 ,  TLINK @ ,
  N>A  N-FWD-RESOLVE  HERE-A N-SELF !  N-COMPILE  A>N
  DOES> N-SHADOW ;
CURRENT !


\ ==== routines that know the image's layout (Iteration 623) ===================
\ Laid at load time, after the prologue, before a build lays anything: a
\ kernel's PRIMITIVE finds them in NTARGET, as native-rt.4's.
N>A
\ The runtime's own data, below the data stack's 64 KB: 64 KB where the
\ asm engine's data chain is rooted (tools/gen-native-os.py: BSS_BASE is
\ N-RTDATA) - arguments, environment, heap pointers, free lists, scratch
\ (634; 64 KB since 635, the chain's save stack alone 32 KB). Free memory,
\ zero as the process starts, off code's cache lines.
N-SIGSTK 65536 - CONSTANT N-RTDATA          \ below the signal stack (639)
NCODE DICT-LIMIT ( --- addr )   \ (672) code grows up to data's region, data to the runtime's
  N-PUSH  rbx [ N-DLIMIT ] mov,  rbx rbx test,  1 F jnz,  rbx N-DSTART # mov,  1 L:  NEND
NCODE DATA-START ( --- addr )   N-PUSH  rbx N-DSTART # mov,  NEND
NCODE DATA-TOP ( --- addr )     N-PUSH  rbx N-RTDATA # mov,  NEND
NCODE DLIMIT-CELL ( --- a-addr )   N-PUSH  rbx N-DLIMIT # mov,  NEND
\ A register loop's r14 and r15 kept on the return stack, under the
\ caller's return address (630): kernel-native.4's CATCH brackets the
\ kernel's with these, so a THROW out of a loop leaves the catcher's own
\ loop as it was.
NCODE (SAVE-LOOP)     rax pop,  r15 push,  r14 push,  rax push,  NEND
NCODE (RESTORE-LOOP)  rax pop,  r14 pop,   r15 pop,   rax push,  NEND
A>N
